// XFAIL: RT-390: `fn cl<T: Clone>(t: &T) -> T { t.clone() }` with T a tuple of references, `cl(&(&a, &b)).1`, is refused with a type error inside std ("expected '&Vec<i64, Gpa>', got 'Vec<i64, Gpa>'", try: `&self.0.clone()`); rustc accepts it and prints the EXPECT line (0.30.2)
// From the review of g302bor2 (form K/k02). Since v0.30.1 at least; the
// release build the same. A tuple of references is Clone through its
// fields' `&T: Clone` (a copy of the reference); the error is in std's
// tuple clone, whose field clone is typed as the Vec's, not the reference's. rustc
// also accepts the drop of a before the use of y: y is `.1`, a borrow of b
// only.
// EXPECT: [2]
fn cl<T: Clone>(t: &T) -> T {
    t.clone()
}

fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let mut a: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    a.push(1);
    let mut b: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    b.push(2);
    let t = (&a, &b);
    let y = cl(&t).1;
    drop(a);
    println("{:?}", y);
}
